  "limongi_channel_notes": {
    "1": "table9 provides wind ejecta at 13--25 Msun and recommended set R is wind-only above 25 Msun.",
    "3": "set R provides terminal ejecta at 13--25 Msun and an explicit full-collapse/zero-terminal-ejecta outcome above 25 Msun; remnant construction is still unapproved."
  },
  "huscher_channel_notes": {
    "2": "The 120 single-star models provide integrated AGB ejecta over 0.8--7 Msun. The separate age table is IMF-weighted population output with a failed stated-normalization check and is not a per-star release history."
  },
  "boccioli_roberti_channel_notes": {
    "1": "Only the F23 single-star Wind branch is counted here. It provides integrated pre-collapse wind ejecta at solar metallicity over 11--45 Msun; channel ownership and interpolation remain unapproved.",
    "3": "F23 single/binary, LC18, and WH07 branch nodes are inventoried independently through their actual source limits. The flattened 11--120 Msun union is evidence-coordinate coverage only; it is not an approved cross-branch grid, fate law, or interpolation domain."
  },
  "doherty_channel_notes": {
    "2": "Only the non-extrapolated VW93 MassExp branch is counted as integrated AGB/SAGB wind return. The 8--9 Msun endpoint exists only at Z >= 0.004; Z=0.001 and 0.0001 stop at 7.5 Msun."
  },
  "stockinger_channel_notes": {
    "3": "The e8.8 ECSN and z9.6/s9.0 low-mass Fe-core CCSN models are discrete event anchors. They have incompatible metallicities and progenitor physics and may not be interpolated into a continuous source grid."
  },
  "sukhbold_channel_notes": {
    "3": "The source-labelled solar Z9.6 branch at 9--12 Msun and the separate W18/N20 engine outcomes at 40--120 Msun are inventoried as distinct branches. Their union is not a continuous mass grid or an approved fate law; the high-mass failed outcomes lack complete remnant/wind records."
  },
  "roberti2024_ultralowz_channel_notes": {
    "3": "The CC BY 4.0 source directly samples Z=0, 3.236e-7, and 3.236e-6, but only at 15 and 25 Msun with an unselected rotation population. Four zero-Z article columns are missing from the official MRTs, 025z600 is quarantined, and no mass or metallicity interpolation is approved."
  },
  "heger_woosley2010_popiii_channel_notes": {
    "3": "The official electronic table densely samples Z=0 over 10--100 Msun, and all source mass nodes are counted as candidate coordinates. The 100--120 Msun runtime edge remains outside this source hull. Explosion energy, piston location, and artificial mixing remain unselected; rotation and neutrino-wind nucleosynthesis are omitted, and no positive-Z interpolation is allowed."
  },
